Z||000000||BENGAL4||10-27-1999||01:02 PM||||Has anyone fabricated their own engine and/or body hoist? If so, could you please give me some details. Thanks.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||fastonpumpgas||10-29-1999||12:58 PM||||I made and engine hoist out of a few 4X4's .  bolted them together at the top in an A-frame.  the only down fall is you cant drrive a car under it, you have to work the motor in.  I made it to orginally lift up my fiero to pull the engine and cradle out the side.  oh yeah I used a come-along to hoist.  Just a though anyway||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-29-1999||07:31 PM||||the best hoist, for cable anyway, is a worm drive boat winch. no matter where you let go of the handle it won't drop and there is no need for a ratchet that can slip. Not sure right off how to mount one on a A frame. I usually use a tripod and attach the winch to a leg.<P>The "factory" engine support goes from the left strut tower to the frame someplace by the battery. I only have a crudy pic of it.<P>exactly what are you planning to do.... we probly have a way to do it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Boxdin||10-31-1999||06:26 PM||||I'm looking for a heavy duty version of the engine holder  currently available. Has anyone used the type currently avail?  Can a guy also lift up the rear end of the car by lifting on the engine holder bar???? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||10-31-1999||06:38 PM||||I lift the rear by removing the rear facia (about 20 min to remove) and shove a long crow bar through the bumper support and hook a chain around both ends. ||||reg||1
